<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <!-- No GeneratePackageOnBuild: it conflicts with `dotnet pack` on a multi-targeted Razor class
         library (NU5026/NU5019 from clean) and the documented publish uses `dotnet pack -o ./nupkg`
         then `nuget push nupkg/...`, which never reads the bin/Release package anyway. -->
    <Title>Blazor Controls</Title>
    <PackageId>WssBlazorControls</PackageId>
	  <AssemblyVersion>10.7.1</AssemblyVersion>
	  <FileVersion>$(AssemblyVersion)</FileVersion>
	  <Version>$(AssemblyVersion)</Version>

    <!-- Build hygiene: the changelog promises 0 warnings — enforce it. CS1591 excepted: the public
         surface is heavily XML-documented but not exhaustively, and missing-comment noise would
         drown real warnings. -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- Ship the XML docs so consumers get IntelliSense from the package. -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

    <!-- Debuggability + reproducibility: SourceLink is built into the .NET 8+ SDK; publish the
         repo URL, ship a .snupkg symbol package, and make CI builds deterministic. -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

    <!-- Catches binary/source breaking changes against the previous published version at pack time. -->
    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>

    <!-- Trimming / WASM AOT support. IsAotCompatible turns on IsTrimmable (the assembly-level
         [AssemblyMetadata("IsTrimmable","True")] that lets a consumer's trimmed publish actually trim
         this library) plus the trim/AOT/single-file Roslyn analyzers. With TreatWarningsAsErrors
         above, any new IL2xxx/IL3xxx regression fails the build. The reflection the library does
         (attribute reads via Field expressions, enum member lookups) is annotated or provably
         rooted — see EnumHelpers/FieldValidationDisplay for the reasoning. -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>

    <!-- Package Metadata -->
    <PackageDescription>A comprehensive library of form controls for Blazor applications, providing consistent, feature-rich input components with built-in validation, accessibility support, and flexible styling options.</PackageDescription>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <!-- SPDX expression (was PackageLicenseFile) so NuGet.org indexes/filters the license properly. -->
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>blazor;controls;forms;validation;accessibility;ui;components;webassembly;server</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>10.7.1 - Breaking: the AntD-style calendar-dropdown date control, formerly EditDatePicker&lt;T&gt;, is renamed to EditDate&lt;T&gt; and is now the default date control -- the previous native-input EditDate&lt;T&gt; is renamed to EditDateNative&lt;T&gt;. A compile-time-obsolete EditDatePicker&lt;T&gt; stub catches stale `&lt;EditDatePicker&gt;` markup with a build error, but a bare existing `&lt;EditDate&gt;` reference that meant the native input still compiles -- it silently renders the calendar dropdown instead; audit every EditDate usage before upgrading and switch to EditDateNative if you need the old native-input behavior. The new EditDate also needs wss-controls.css and the lazily-imported wss-picker.js (previously only edit-controls.css), so an app linking just edit-controls.css now renders an unstyled date field with no dropdown. Narrower breaks alongside it: INotificationService.Success/Info/Warning/Error now return Guid instead of void (pass it to Remove to dismiss a sticky notification programmatically) -- a source break only for a custom INotificationService implementation; ReadOnlyValue.IsLabelHidden is replaced by HasLabelElement (inverted meaning); the always-inert FormLabel.IdPrefix and FieldValidationDisplay.IdPrefix are removed; WasmMessageContainer/WasmNotificationContainer now throw on Blazor Server (including InteractiveAuto's server phase) instead of silently leaking one user's toasts to every circuit -- switch to the scoped IMessageService/INotificationService path if this fires; EditDateRange.FieldCssClass changes from a protected property to a protected method (affects only an out-of-repo subclass, none known); and both the password and read-only-mask reveal toggles now keep a constant accessible name with aria-pressed carrying the state, instead of a name that flips with the state -- a Playwright/test-selector break only, not a runtime one. Security: EditString's read-only link mode now mirrors the browser's own URL preprocessing before checking scheme, closing two javascript: bypasses (an embedded tab/CR/LF, a leading C0 control byte) and rejecting a protocol-relative URL (//host/path) that used to resolve cross-origin; rel="noopener noreferrer" now covers every UrlTarget except _self/_parent/_top, not just _blank, closing a reverse-tabnabbing gap on named targets (a test asserting no rel on a named target needs updating). Read-only password/masked fields no longer disclose their value: a disabled field's toggle can no longer reveal it, the reveal state no longer survives a read-only round trip, an IsPassword flip, or a swapped bound record, an all-whitespace MaskText now masks instead of silently printing the raw value, and FormOptions.ShowBoundValues now redacts password fields instead of echoing them. New (Edit Controls): EditDate&lt;T&gt; gains Size (SelectSize, wss-picker-sm/lg) and ParsingErrorMessage (default "The {0} field must be a date.", surfaced via its own ValidationMessageStore when typed text isn't a date at all) -- both added to the picker before the rename above, so EditDate is a genuine superset of the old EditDatePicker, not a regression; EditDate deliberately has no UpdateOn (a picker commits on selection/parse, not per keystroke -- use EditDateNative for that axis); UpdateTrigger enum + UpdateOn parameter (plus FormDefaults.UpdateOn) to choose commit-on-keystroke vs. commit-on-blur/Enter for EditString/EditTextArea/EditNumber/EditDateNative/the Radio "Other" box; six new model attributes ([Placeholder], [MinValue]/[MaxValue], [Autocomplete], [Step], [BoolText], [Rows], [FileConstraints]) so field-semantic markup can live on the model instead of every call site, honored with a uniform precedence (markup parameter -&gt; model attribute -&gt; DataAnnotations fallback -&gt; control default) across every scalar and date control. New (UI Kit): DatePicker/DateRangePicker gain Size (SelectSize, wss-picker-sm/lg), the same parameter EditDate forwards; Select.AriaErrorMessage, forwarded by EditSelectSearch/EditMultiSelect, plus aria-errormessage on EditFile; a new Select.AdditionalAttributes splat (previously an unmatched attribute on &lt;Select&gt; threw); Table gains eight localizable label parameters covering its last hardcoded English strings (selection checkboxes, pagers, sort/filter buttons). Changed: default checkbox/radio label spacing now matches AntD's 8px flex-row gap for every EditBool/EditCheckedStringList/EditCheckedEnumList/EditRadioString/EditRadioEnum/EditRadio label, not just the UseStyledCheckbox variant -- a visible default-rendering change for every consumer; EditSelectSearch.Placeholder/EditMultiSelect.Placeholder are now string? (previously string, defaulted to "Please select"); unmatched attributes (inputmode, readonly, spellcheck, data-*, title, extra aria-*) on any scalar Edit* control now actually render instead of being silently swallowed, landing on the field element (or .edit-control-wrapper for style) -- a control with no extra attributes still renders byte-identical markup; a runtime Id/IdPrefix change now re-targets the whole control (FormLabel's for, aria-describedby/errormessage, FormOptions registration) instead of leaving it wired to its original id; EditString/EditTextArea's Clear() now writes an empty string instead of null, matching manual deletion and closing a HidingMode.WhenNull clear-and-unmount trap. Fixed: a large internal multi-round audit landed dozens more accessibility, correctness and DRY fixes across the whole library -- highlights: Tabs keeps its declared tab order and keyboard focus across conditional insertion/removal; Table column order no longer drifts on sort/filter/paging, filter-pruned values no longer filter invisibly, and a runtime column-parameter change now actually re-renders; both date pickers enforce Disabled while their panel is open, drop half-typed text on an external value change, and no longer crash on Mode="Week" near DateTime's own range limits; EditFile's upload-rejection messages and hover state no longer outlive their upload or survive going disabled; EditRadioEnum's preserved "Other" text no longer leaks onto a swapped bound record; an empty EditDisplay no longer collapses to zero height; RTL logical-property and prefers-reduced-motion coverage extended across both stylesheets; several WCAG 1.4.3/1.4.11 contrast and 2.5.8 hit-target fixes; the new flex checkbox/radio labels are hardened against a consumer's own input flex/margin resets; EditSelectEnum ports EditSelectString's no-JS selected-option fallback for prerender/no-JS rendering; the Select engine's value-to-label lookup is unified across Select/EditSelectSearch/EditMultiSelect, fixing label drift on a duplicate-valued option list; SearchInput's clear/search buttons no longer collapse under a consumer's button height reset; the JS overlay positioning helpers are consolidated, fixing inconsistent dropdown/panel flip-to-fit behavior. See the README changelog for the complete list. Internal: extensive DRY/refactoring passes (shared control-base classes, JS module and overlay-positioning consolidation, CSS token consolidation, hoisted e2e scaffolding) and dependency/test-infra bumps (ASP.NET Core Components, bUnit 2.x, Playwright) -- no consumer-facing API or behavior change beyond what's called out above.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>dcblakesley</Authors>
    <Company>WSS</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2025 WssBlazorControls</Copyright>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Include README and the package icon (license is declared via PackageLicenseExpression) -->
    <None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="10.0.10" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
